  "prefLabel": "Rko 218.01 Retention of Decisions and Verbatim Recordings of Adjudicative Proceedings",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Rko 218.01 Retention of Decisions and Verbatim Recordings of Adjudicative Proceedings.\n\n(a) The office shall keep all decisions and orders which it has issued in its records for at least 5 years following the date of issuance, unless the director of the division of records management and archives of the department of state sets a different retention period pursuant to rules adopted under RSA 5:40.\n\n(b) Pursuant to RSA 541-A:30-a,VII, the office shall retain a verbatim recording of all oral adjudicative proceedings for at least 30 days after the opportunity for all administrative and judicial appeals has been exhausted.",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/rko100-200.html"
